GCC runtime libraries in the x86_64-linux-musl gem of elelem-llama
==================================================================

Alpine Linux has no C++ runtime until one is installed, so this gem
carries the one it was built with. Two files in ext/elelem/llama/native
are not part of elelem-llama and are not under its MIT license:

  libstdc++-elelem.so.6   the GNU C++ standard library (libstdc++.so.6)
  libgcc_s-elelem.so.1    the GCC support library (libgcc_s.so.1)

They are the GNU Compiler Collection runtime libraries, Copyright (C)
Free Software Foundation, Inc., licensed under the GNU General Public
License, version 3 or later, with the GCC Runtime Library Exception,
version 3.1 (SPDX: GPL-3.0-or-later WITH GCC-exception-3.1). The texts
of both are beside this file: COPYING3 and COPYING.RUNTIME.

Where the binaries come from
----------------------------

They are the files of two Alpine Linux 3.22 packages, x86_64, built
from the aport main/gcc:

  libstdc++-14.2.0-r6     usr/lib/libstdc++.so.6.0.33
  libgcc-14.2.0-r6        usr/lib/libgcc_s.so.1

Where the source is
-------------------

GCC 14.2.0, as released:

  https://gcc.gnu.org/pub/gcc/releases/gcc-14.2.0/gcc-14.2.0.tar.xz

The patches and the build script (APKBUILD) Alpine applied to it, at
the commit that built these packages:

  https://gitlab.alpinelinux.org/alpine/aports/-/tree/fbf60319be3bbaf6dd32ef55cc6fb7189e05c266/main/gcc

What elelem-llama changed
-------------------------

Nothing in the code. The files are renamed, and patchelf rewrites the
names in their ELF headers to match, so that this copy never stands in
for the libstdc++.so.6 or libgcc_s.so.1 of the system it is installed
on:

  patchelf --set-soname libstdc++-elelem.so.6 libstdc++-elelem.so.6
  patchelf --set-soname libgcc_s-elelem.so.1 libgcc_s-elelem.so.1

and then, on these two and on every other library beside them:

  patchelf --replace-needed libstdc++.so.6 libstdc++-elelem.so.6 \
           --replace-needed libgcc_s.so.1 libgcc_s-elelem.so.1 <library>

The code that does it is ext/elelem/llama/cxx_runtime.rb in

  https://github.com/elelem-sh/llama
